llvm-3.7.1 forward port: a select's expensive operand is sunk into a branch (the guarded division)

This patch CHANGES CODE GENERATION where one arm of a two-way choice is a
division or remainder: `v != 0 ? 1 / v : 0`. 3.7.1's SimplifyCFG speculates
the division into a select and its code generation keeps the select
(`vdivss` first, then `vcmpneqss`/`vcmpltss` and `vandps`); the base tests
first and divides in the arm (`vucomiss; je`, `vdivss` behind the branch).
Upstream reached that in three commits, all first released in 3.8.0, each
ported whole (tests left out):
  r248439 (13e8bbc23735, 2015-09-23) "set div/rem default values to
    'expensive' in TargetTransformInfo's cost model": FDiv, FRem, SDiv, SRem,
    UDiv and URem cost TCC_Expensive in getOperationCost (applies as is);
  r250743 (69a50a1e17c9, 2015-10-19) "[CGP] transform select instructions
    into branches and sink expensive operands": CodeGenPrepare forms a branch
    from a select with a single-use, safe-to-speculate operand of that cost
    and moves the operand into the arm. Its include hunk applies as is; the
    other three are written in by hand against 3.7.1's text, which lacks
    upstream's intervening NFC tidy-ups (the one-use test of the compare as
    an early return; `optimizeSelectInst`'s lower-case name; the iterator
    passed to PHINode::Create): the statements are upstream's;
  r255660 (38a022623a6b, 2015-12-15) "[SimplifyCFG] allow speculation of
    exactly one expensive instruction (PR24818)": SimplifyCFG still makes the
    select (as 3.7.1 does today), now that the cost says expensive, so the
    IR up to CodeGenPrepare is unchanged (applies with offsets, fuzz 2 on
    the option's hunk).
Not ported, same sequence: r253573 (4699b8ab6acf, 2015-11-19, "[CGP]
despeculate expensive cttz/ctlz intrinsics"): a separate transform for
targets where the count is not cheap to speculate; no row asks for it.

Swept alone over the game module built by the installed 3.7.1 (round 273B,
5,496 rows, 6,656 functions): 10 functions change; 7 rows become equal
(5,297 to 5,304: 0x1b1090, 0x4ada80, 0x1064290, 0x13d29d0, 0x13d2a40,
0x13d6330, 0x13d63a0) and none is lost.

